---
import { getCollection, render } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import TierTag from '../components/TierTag.astro';
import Annotation from '../components/Annotation.astro';
import { t, localePath } from '../lib/i18n.js';

const locale = 'en';

const all = await getCollection('multiSite', (e) => e.id.startsWith(`${locale}/`));

/** Render each body once, up front: Astro cannot await inside the template. */
const rendered = await Promise.all(
  all.map(async (entry) => ({ entry, Content: (await render(entry)).Content }))
);
const by = (kind) =>
  rendered
    .filter((r) => r.entry.data.kind === kind)
    .sort((a, b) => (a.entry.data.number ?? a.entry.data.order) - (b.entry.data.number ?? b.entry.data.order));

const failureModes = by('failure-mode');
const additions = by('addition');
const modules = by('module');

/**
 * Artifact titles come from the artifacts collection where that pass has
 * landed; until then, fall back to a readable label built from the slug.
 */
const artifacts = await getCollection('artifacts', (e) => e.id.startsWith(`${locale}/`));
const titleBySlug = new Map(artifacts.map((a) => [a.id.split('/').slice(1).join('/'), a.data.title]));
const artifactLabel = (slug) =>
  titleBySlug.get(slug) ??
  slug
    .split('-')
    .map((word) => (word === 'ai' ? 'AI' : word))
    .join(' ')
    .replace(/^./, (c) => c.toUpperCase());

const lede =
  'The design constraint that governs the rest of this site — no lawyer, no IT department, twenty minutes — is right for the modal provider and wrong for a fourteen-site organization with an HR director and outside counsel.';
const description =
  'Governance structure, model contract language and a defensible answer for a board: what a chain, a large center or a Head Start grantee with delegate agencies has to add.';
---
<BaseLayout title={t(locale, 'nav.multiSite')} description={description} locale={locale}>
  <PageHeader
    caption="The multi-site track"
    title={t(locale, 'nav.multiSite')}
    lede={lede}
    locale={locale}
    lastUpdated="2026-09-10"
  />

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Larger operators are not a smaller problem. They are a different one, and the field
    has no guidance for them at all.
  </p>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    A large center, a chain, or a Head Start grantee with delegate agencies has something
    the single site does not: the capacity to actually govern this. An HR director. Outside
    counsel. Someone whose job includes procurement. What it does not have is anyone telling
    it how.
  </p>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    So this page is not a longer version of the small-provider material, and you should not
    read it as one. If you are running fourteen sites you are not looking for a policy
    template — you are looking for a governance structure, model contract language, and a
    defensible answer for your board. That is what is below. Everything in
    <a class="govuk-link" href={localePath(locale, '/policies')}>the policies to adopt</a>
    still applies; these nine additions sit on top of it, and each one exists because it does
    not make sense below a certain size.
  </p>

  <nav class="govuk-!-margin-bottom-8" aria-label={t(locale, 'label.onThisPage')}>
    <h2 class="govuk-heading-s">{t(locale, 'label.onThisPage')}</h2>
    <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number govuk-body-s">
      <li><a class="govuk-link" href="#failure-modes">Two ways this goes wrong at scale</a></li>
      <li><a class="govuk-link" href="#additions">What the multi-site track adds</a></li>
      <li><a class="govuk-link" href="#delegate-agencies">Head Start grantees with delegate agencies</a></li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="failure-modes">Two ways this goes wrong at scale</h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Left alone, these organizations fail in two opposite directions, and both are worse than
    they look. One is documented as caution. The other is not documented at all.
  </p>

  <div class="govuk-warning-text">
    <span class="govuk-warning-text__icon" aria-hidden="true">!</span>
    <strong class="govuk-warning-text__text">
      <span class="govuk-visually-hidden">Warning</span>
      A blanket ban is not a safety posture. It is an unmonitored one.
    </strong>
  </div>

  {failureModes.map(({ entry, Content }) => (
    <section class="govuk-!-margin-bottom-8" id={entry.id.split('/').slice(1).join('/')}>
      <h3 class="govuk-heading-s">{entry.data.title}</h3>
      <p class="govuk-body-l">{entry.data.summary}</p>
      <div class="govuk-body app-prose"><Content /></div>
      {entry.data.relatedArtifacts.length > 0 && (
        <Annotation label={t(locale, 'label.relatedArtifacts')}>
          <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">
            {entry.data.relatedArtifacts.map((slug) => (
              <li>
                <a class="govuk-link" href={localePath(locale, `/artifacts/${slug}`)}>
                  {artifactLabel(slug)}
                </a>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </Annotation>
      )}
    </section>
  ))}

  <hr class="govuk-section-break govuk-section-break--l govuk-section-break--visible" />

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="additions">What the multi-site track adds</h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Nine things, on top of everything a single site already does. Each exists because it does
    not make sense below a certain size, and each one is aimed at the same target: closing the
    distance between what the policy says and what is actually running at site eleven.
  </p>

  <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number govuk-!-margin-bottom-8">
    {additions.map(({ entry }) => (
      <li>
        <a class="govuk-link" href={`#addition-${entry.data.number}`}>{entry.data.title}</a>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>

  {additions.map(({ entry, Content }) => (
    <section class="govuk-!-margin-bottom-8" id={`addition-${entry.data.number}`}>
      <h3 class="govuk-heading-s govuk-!-margin-bottom-2">
        <span class="govuk-caption-m">{entry.data.number} of 9</span>
        {entry.data.title}
      </h3>
      <p class="govuk-body-l">{entry.data.summary}</p>

      {entry.data.number === 1 && (
        <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-bottom-4">
          <span class="govuk-!-margin-right-2"><TierTag tier={1} locale={locale} withName={true} /></span>
          <span class="govuk-!-margin-right-2"><TierTag tier={2} locale={locale} withName={true} /></span>
          <span class="govuk-!-margin-right-2"><TierTag tier={3} locale={locale} withName={true} /></span>
        </p>
      )}

      <div class="govuk-body app-prose"><Content /></div>

      {entry.data.number === 3 && (
        <p class="govuk-body">
          <a class="govuk-link" href={localePath(locale, '/vendors')}>The ten questions to ask a vendor</a>
          are where a single center starts. The rider is where a large one starts.
        </p>
      )}

      {entry.data.number === 5 && (
        <p class="govuk-body">
          <a class="govuk-link" href={localePath(locale, '/law')}>The regulatory crosswalk</a>
          carries the state layer you would be setting that standard against.
        </p>
      )}

      {entry.data.relatedArtifacts.length > 0 && (
        <Annotation label={t(locale, 'label.relatedArtifacts')}>
          <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">
            {entry.data.relatedArtifacts.map((slug) => (
              <li>
                <a class="govuk-link" href={localePath(locale, `/artifacts/${slug}`)}>
                  {artifactLabel(slug)}
                </a>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </Annotation>
      )}
    </section>
  ))}

  <hr class="govuk-section-break govuk-section-break--l govuk-section-break--visible" />

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="delegate-agencies">Head Start grantees with delegate agencies</h2>

  {modules.map(({ entry, Content }) => (
    <div class="govuk-inset-text">
      <p class="govuk-body-l">{entry.data.summary}</p>
      <div class="app-prose"><Content /></div>
      {entry.data.relatedArtifacts.length > 0 && (
        <Annotation label={t(locale, 'label.relatedArtifacts')}>
          <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">
            {entry.data.relatedArtifacts.map((slug) => (
              <li>
                <a class="govuk-link" href={localePath(locale, `/artifacts/${slug}`)}>
                  {artifactLabel(slug)}
                </a>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </Annotation>
      )}
    </div>
  ))}

  <hr class="govuk-section-break govuk-section-break--l govuk-section-break--visible" />

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="what-does-not-change">What does not change</h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Different artifacts, a different page, a different reader — and the same
    <a class="govuk-link" href={localePath(locale, '/principles')}>principles</a> and the same
    <a class="govuk-link" href={localePath(locale, '/bright-lines')}>bright lines</a> as
    everywhere else on this site. A charter with delegated authority, a rider your counsel
    negotiated and a quarterly item on the board agenda do not buy an exemption from any of
    them. They are how an organization of your size keeps them true at every site at once.
  </p>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Scale changes who decides, how fast, on what evidence and with what leverage. It does not
    change what is allowed.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
